---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Privacy | fallback.pics"
  description="Privacy information for fallback.pics fallback image infrastructure."
  keywords="fallback.pics privacy, placeholder image privacy, fallback image service"
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  heading="Privacy"
  intro="fallback.pics is designed for privacy-conscious fallback image delivery. Standard image generation uses URL parameters such as dimensions, colors, and optional text. It does not require customer source image uploads or client-side cookies for image delivery."
>
  <section class="content-section">
    <p>
      Custom text can appear in URLs, browser history, CDN logs, and application logs. Do not place secrets, tokens, regulated data, or private customer information in fallback image URLs.
    </p>
    <p>
      Website pages may use Google Analytics when a measurement ID is configured, and the image API can send server-side aggregate request events for direct Worker URL calls. API analytics strip query strings before sending URL metadata, so custom <code>text=</code> values are not forwarded to Google Analytics.
    </p>
    <p>
      For enterprise privacy, security, or data-processing questions, review the <a href="/api">API Reference</a>, <a href="https://status.fallback.pics">Status</a>, and <a href="https://github.com/abhijeetpratapsingh/fallback-pics">GitHub</a>, or contact <a href="mailto:support@fallback.pics">support@fallback.pics</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>
